everyone knows green goblin from the  spider-man movies but it's a special few  who know about his time in spider-punk's  spider army during the edge of  spider-geddon curious what we're talking  about keep watching  nowadays it might seem like common  knowledge that norman osborne is the  green goblin but the goblins identity  was once actually a mystery to readers  from the character's first appearance in  amazing spider-man number 14 it would be  two years 25 issues and one major artist  change before the green goblin was  unmasked that artist change even helped  feed an urban legend about the goblin  one that has survived for years amazing  spider-man number 38 was spidey  co-creator steve ditko's final issue as  the comics artist john ramita senior  replaced ditko with amazing spider-man  number 39 which happens to be the issue  in which goblin's identity is revealed  goblin being unmasked as soon as ditko  left the title led many fans to believe  that ditko was against osborne being  green goblin and that this was why he  left spider-man's other co-creator has  seemed to confirm half of this fan  theory in a 2011 issue of the magazine  alter ego stan lee said ditko wanted  goblin to be just some character that we  had never seen before but lee insisted  that would be cheating readers however  by the time ditko left amazing  spider-man he and lee were embroiled in  so many financial conflicts that ditco's  departure from the title was inevitable  regardless of any creative differences  that said in a 2009 essay ditko not only  denied lee's claims that he was against  osborne being the goblin but says he  always knew osborne would be the goblin  and that he made plenty of creative  choices to facilitate that future reveal  norman osborne is hardly the only  character to bear the name green goblin  in fact while he's the original most  memorable and most enduring version of  the character he's only one of five  different characters to have used the  name just as norman's son harry becomes  new goblin in 2007's spider-man 3 harry  also assumes the name of green goblin in  1974's amazing spider-man number 136  after discovering peter parker was  spider-man  look at little goblin junior  gonna cry  the third goblin is dr bart hamilton a  psychiatrist who treats harry osborn  hamilton uses hypnosis to learn green  goblin's secrets including the location  of his hideout and equipment visiting  the hideout hamilton gives in to  temptation and becomes the next goblin  beginning in 1978's amazing spider-man  number 176 green goblin number four  tries his hand at the hero business phil  urich son of daily bugle reporter ben  urich recovers the goblin equipment  after harry osborne's death and even  enjoys a short-lived solo title eurek  retires after his equipment is damaged  beyond repair during the 1996 onslaught  event after returning from the dead for  a few decades norman osborne orders the  creation of a genetically engineered  minion designed to be the new green  goblin in 2000's peter parker spider-man  number 18. he dresses as the goblin and  acts like the goblin all to help osborne  convince the world he was never the  green goblin in the first place  eventually green goblin became more than  just spider-man's enemy how well as it  happened he was helped out by a bunch of  green skinned guys with pointy ears  during the 2006 civil war event norman  osborne is appointed director of a new  version of the thunderbolts a group  tasked with capturing unregistered  superheroes osborne's thunderbolts  include villains who are a little  nastier than the team is used to  including the kill crazy villain  bullseye and the deadly symbiote venom  osborne's leadership role in the  thunderbolts puts him in a position to  be in the right place at the right time  when secret invasion comes along focused  on the shape-shifting scrolls secret  invasion has most of marvel's heroes  uniting against this new alien threat  osborne later succeeds in gaining the  public's trust by shooting and killing  the skrull queen varanki when the dust  settles tony stark is blamed for the  scroll infiltration and ousted as  director of shield while osborne is made  the head of the new military force  hammer from there his power keeps on  growing  when green goblin gains control of  hammer the superhero registration act is  still in effect and most of the  surviving former avengers are considered  outlaws osborne takes advantage of this  situation and forms his own team of dark  avengers most of osborne's dark avengers  are villains renamed and rebranded as  the replacements for more traditional  avengers bullseye is disguised as  hawkeye dawkin as wolverine venom as  spider-man and moonstone as ms marvel  novar aka marvel boy joins the team as a  new captain marvel the only holdouts  from pre-osborn avengers teams are the  mentally unstable sentry and the morally  questionable war god aries osborne's  influence is finally put to bed at the  conclusion of the 2010 line-wide event  siege in which osborne leads a failed  invasion of asgard and is finally  arrested and imprisoned for his crimes  it tested well with focus groups all  right i am iron patriots  if you've seen iron man 3 then you'll  already know the name iron patriot what  you may not know is that in the comics  iron patriot originally had nothing to  do with colonel james rhodes  combining the design of stark's iron man  armor with the colors of captain america  norman osborne creates the iron patriot  armor so he can use it to lead his dark  avengers the armor gives him most of  iron man's abilities though unlike  stark's armor it isn't based on repulsor  technology norman also creates the  american sun armor for his son harry but  the younger osborne would eventually  discover that norman did it just so he  could eventually kill harry in order to  create public sympathy for himself  norman remains iron patriot until his  plans fall apart in siege he eventually  escapes from the raft and forms a new  team of dark avengers in the hopes of  recapturing his old suit and getting his  revenge on the heroes who defeated him  he fails of course and soon after  resumes his life as the green goblin  norman osborne's most sickeningly  powerful transformation comes at the end  of 2018's amazing spider-man number 798  osborne is one of the first people to  figure out peter parker is spider-man  but the events of the 2007 storyline one  more day takes that knowledge away from  him in amazing spider-man number 797  when j jonah jameson mentions green  goblin's killing of gwen stacy the words  spark something in osborne and cause him  to remember who spider-man is with this  new revelation goblin demands spidey  quit being a hero or he'll kill all the  important people in parker's life  osborne also attacks the offices of the  daily bugle and after an intense battle  with spider-man winds up impaled on  debris spidey thinks goblin's dying but  the issue ends with the carnage symbiote  appearing and bonding with osborne to  create the red goblin as the red goblin  osbourne is more powerful than ever and  doesn't even suffer the usual symbiote  vulnerabilities to fire and sound red  goblin continues the hunt for parker's  loved ones and spidey is only able to  prevent the killing of ant-may and mj  with the help of venom anti-venom and  the superior octopus borrowing venom's  symbiote and allied with his old friend  flash thompson spidey is finally able to  defeat the red goblin although flash is  killed during the battle  the 2014 marvel comics event  spider-verse introduced dozens of  alternate reality versions of spider-man  then in 2018 spider-geddon brought in  even more alternate spideys including a  norman osborne version of the character  edge of spider-geddon number four  introduces the spider-man of earth 44145  in that reality norman osborne gained  spider abilities instead of peter parker  and even grew four extra arms in the  process this version of norman osborne  is forcefully recruited into the new  spider army by spider punk but by the  end of spider geddon it seems clear that  everyone would have been better off  leaving him at home allying himself only  with spider's man of earth 11580  the osborne spidey abandons the spider  army and chooses to destroy the web of  life and destiny that allows the  different spider heroes to travel  between other realities after  spider-geddon this character acts as the  final adversary for the reformed auto  octavius in the 2019 volume of superior  spider-man  most recently in the comics norman  osborne has turned to the side of the  angels though you could make the  argument it wasn't by his own choice  shortly after being made the director of  ravencroft institute by mayor wilson  fisk osborne finds himself in the  crosshairs of a resurrected vigilante  the supernatural villain kindred had  brought the sin eater back to life and  this time he has powers worthy of his  namesake rather than just killing his  prey the new sin eater can wipe away his  target's sins which is precisely what he  does to norman in 2020's amazing  spider-man number 50. while he believes  senator is going to kill him norman  instead wakes to find his evil urges  have disappeared replaced only with  remorse for everything he's done  understandably it takes spider-man a  while to accept that osborne's changes  are genuine and the wall crawler beats  the heck out of him in 2021's amazing  spider-man number 57 spidey fortunately  stops himself before he goes too far for  the time being osborne seems to be on  the right side of things in fact he does  what little he can to help spider-man  during the 2021 sinister war event but  considering who he is it's probably only  a matter of time before the green goblin  flies again  nearly two decades after 2002's  spider-man helped usher in the dominance  of superheroes on the big screen willem  dafoe had some pretty wonderful things  to say about his experience playing the  green goblin speaking to gq in february  2019 defoe talked about how the osborne  green goblin duality appealed to him  you could play these scenes where  it would switch from comedy to drama  in a line  as an example defoe singled out the  scene in which osborne and green goblin  have a conversation with one another in  a mirror he told gq that director sam  raimi even gave him robert lewis  stevenson's novel the strange case of dr  jekyll and mr hyde to read for the scene  during his sit-down with gq defoe  repeatedly mentions how much fun he had  during his experience on spider-man and  it must have been worth it too  considering the role's considerable  physical challenges in a  behind-the-scenes feature on the  spider-man dvd defoe claimed to have  endured between 40 and 50 hours of  fittings of the goblin suit before the  design was finalized defoe said it was  really uncomfortable to wear it was so  tight and so heavy that after a whole  day in that thing you felt like you had  just gone 12 rounds  early in june 2019 the anonymous leaker  known as roger wardell unleashed a  torrent of supposed leaks about mcu's  phase 4. while many of these leaks  remain unconfirmed it's only fair to  mention that this same person leaked  accurate details about avengers end game  months before the movie's release among  other things wardell had some major  claims about the green goblin according  to the alleged leaks phase 4's primary  antagonist won't be a purple guy from  outer space but someone much closer to  home yes wardell claims that norman  osborne will supposedly serve as the  next big bad of the mcu of course it's  now known that willem dafoe's version of  green goblin is on his way to the mcu  defoe will reprise the villainous role  in spider-man no way home but it remains  to be seen whether he'll replace thanos  as marvel's main villain considering  osborne and the other spider-man  villains appearing will be travelers  from other parts of the multiverse one  of the more likely outcomes of the story  would seem to be their return to their  respective realities not only that but  jonathan major's king the conqueror has  been frequently cited as the true big  bad of phase four but it's likely that  kevin feige and company won't be able to  resist introducing their own version of  norman osborn at some point or another  and who knows what might happen with him  only time will tell check out one of our  newest videos right here plus even more  looper videos about your favorite movies  and tv shows are coming soon subscribe  to our youtube channel and hit the bell  so you don't miss a single one  [Music]

